{"title":"Avionics Engineer Roadmap","role":"Avionics Engineer","summary":"An Avionics Engineer designs, develops, integrates, tests, and maintains the electronic and computer-based systems used in aircraft, spacecraft, launch vehicles, and unmanned aerial systems.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Space Technology / Avionics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Avionics Engineer designs, develops, integrates, tests, and maintains the electronic and computer-based systems used in aircraft, spacecraft, launch vehicles, and unmanned aerial systems."},{"type":"p","text":"In the space sector, avionics can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Flight computers"},{"text":"Guidance, navigation and control electronics"},{"text":"Telemetry and telecommand"},{"text":"Communication systems"},{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Inertial measurement systems"},{"text":"Power electronics"},{"text":"Data acquisition"},{"text":"Embedded systems"},{"text":"On-board software"},{"text":"RF systems"},{"text":"Navigation systems"},{"text":"Fault detection and protection"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a highly interdisciplinary career combining electronics + embedded systems + control systems + communication + software + aerospace/space engineering."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build electronics, embedded systems, control, communication and aerospace fundamentals; enter as Avionics Engineer, Embedded Engineer, Electronics Engineer or related graduate engineer."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Progress toward Avionics Design Engineer, Flight Electronics Engineer, GNC/Control Engineer, Embedded Systems Engineer or Avionics Test Engineer."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move into Lead Avionics Engineer, Systems Integration Lead, Avionics Architect or Technical Project Lead."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Chief/Principal Avionics Engineer, Systems Engineering Manager, Avionics Program Manager or Space Systems Technical Leadership."}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Electronics, Mathematics & Programming","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The first year should establish strong engineering fundamentals."},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Differential equations"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Probability and statistics"},{"text":"Numerical methods"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Physics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Electricity and magnetism"},{"text":"Waves"},{"text":"Optics"},{"text":"Modern physics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Electronics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Circuit theory"},{"text":"Analog electronics"},{"text":"Digital electronics"},{"text":"Semiconductor fundamentals"},{"text":"Logic gates"},{"text":"Microelectronics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"C"},{"text":"C++"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Basic data structures and algorithms"},{"text":"C/C++ is particularly important for embedded and real-time systems."}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Embedded Systems & Control","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The second year should focus on the electronics and computing systems that form the foundation of avionics."},{"type":"h","text":"Embedded systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microcontrollers"},{"text":"Microprocessors"},{"text":"GPIO"},{"text":"Timers"},{"text":"Interrupts"},{"text":"ADC/DAC"},{"text":"UART"},{"text":"SPI"},{"text":"I²C"},{"text":"CAN"},{"text":"Memory systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Operating concepts"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Real-time systems"},{"text":"Embedded operatin